<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pahlavas</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pahlavas is the name used in ancient Indian texts, such as the Manusmriti, the epics and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puranas">Puranas</a>, for a people from the north-west usually identified with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parthian-empire">Parthians</a>, especially the Indo-Parthian rulers of the first century CE. They are often listed with the Shakas and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yavana">Yavanas</a> as foreigners. A theory linking the South Indian Pallava dynasty with them on the basis of the name has little support.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pahlavas.jpg" alt="Pahlavas" width="320" height="496" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Smith, Vincent Arthur, 1848-1920 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mauryan_head_from_Sarnath.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
